#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:1
msgid "Relational Charts: Synastry and Composite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:3
msgid ""
"Relational charts analyse two people's charts together rather than in "
"isolation. Ketu provides three modules for this: `ketu.charts` builds the"
" individual charts, `ketu.synastry` compares them aspect by aspect, and "
"`ketu.composite` derives a midpoint chart that represents the "
"relationship itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:5
msgid "Building Charts with compute_chart"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:7
msgid ""
"`compute_chart` is the central function for natal chart calculation. It "
"calculates all 14 body positions, twelve house cusps, the four angles, "
"and the full aspect matrix in a single call, returning a `CHART_DTYPE` "
"structured array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:13 ../../source/relational_charts.md:78
msgid "**Parameters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:15
msgid "`jd` — Julian Day (float, UTC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:16
msgid "`lat` / `lon` — geographic latitude and longitude in degrees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:17
msgid "`system` — house system (default `\"placidus\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:18
msgid "`aspects` — aspect set spec (`None` uses the default classical set)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/relational_charts.md:19
msgid ""
"`polar_fallback` — high-latitude fallback behaviour (see [House "
"Systems](houses.md))"
msgstr ""

